1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,885
Say the color of the words!

2
00:00:04,935 --> 00:00:07,255
Don't read the word —
say its COLOR out loud

3
00:00:07,305 --> 00:00:10,625
For this one, the answer is "red"!

4
00:00:10,675 --> 00:00:14,395
Say the colors!

5
00:00:14,445 --> 00:00:17,395
Easy, right?

6
00:00:17,445 --> 00:00:21,915
Now the words and colors don't match.
Say the colors!

7
00:00:21,965 --> 00:00:24,915
Not the word — the color!

8
00:00:24,965 --> 00:00:28,915
Tongue-tied?

9
00:00:28,965 --> 00:00:33,485
Red, green, blue / yellow, green, yellow
red, blue, yellow

10
00:00:33,535 --> 00:00:35,455
When you see a word,
two things start in your brain at once

11
00:00:35,505 --> 00:00:38,255
You've practiced reading so much
that it's automatic and super fast

12
00:00:38,305 --> 00:00:40,855
"Blue" arrives first
and crashes into "red"

13
00:00:40,905 --> 00:00:44,825
Your brain slows down because it has to hold back the reading
and pick the color

14
00:00:44,875 --> 00:00:49,425
Like riding a bike, things you're used to
happen before you even think

15
00:00:49,475 --> 00:00:51,675
This is called the "Stroop effect"

16
00:00:51,725 --> 00:00:54,175
NEXT: A sound that keeps rising forever?
